<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Arranging repeated digits and coin-toss outcome sequences</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>(a)</b> How many unique numbers can be formed by arranging all of the digits \({@pA@}\) threes, \({@pB@}\) sevens, and \({@pC@}\) nines (all in one number)?</p>
<p>Number of arrangements = [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>

<p><b>(b)</b> A coin is flipped \({@pnc@}\) times. How many different sequences of outcomes have exactly \({@pH@}\) Heads and \({@pT@}\) Tails?</p>
<p>Number of sequences = [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>

<p>When arranging \(n\) items that contain identical groups of sizes \(r_1, r_2, \dots\), divide \(n!\) by the factorial of each repeated group:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle P = \frac{n!}{r_1! \times r_2! \times \cdots}\)</p>

<p><b>Part (a): Arranging {@pA@} threes, {@pB@} sevens, and {@pC@} nines</b><br>
Total number of digits: \(n = {@pA@} + {@pB@} + {@pC@} = {@pn@}\). Substitute into the formula, expand \({@pn@}!\) until it matches \({@d1@}!\), and cancel:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle P = \frac{{@pn@}!}{{@pA@}! \times {@pB@}! \times {@pC@}!} = \frac{{@num1_factors@} \times {@d1@}!}{{@d1@}! \times ({@den1_d2@}) \times ({@den1_d3@})} = \frac{{@num1_val@}}{{@den1_val@}} = {@ta1@}\)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\(\displaystyle \boxed{ \text{Number of arrangements} = {@ta1@} }\)</p>

<p><b>Part (b): Sequences with {@pH@} Heads and {@pT@} Tails in {@pnc@} flips</b><br>
Total number of flips: \(n = {@pH@} + {@pT@} = {@pnc@}\). Treating the identical Heads and identical Tails as two repeated groups, expand \({@pnc@}!\) until it matches \({@big2@}!\) and cancel:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle P = \frac{{@pnc@}!}{{@pH@}! \times {@pT@}!} = \frac{{@num2_factors@} \times {@big2@}!}{{@big2@}! \times ({@den2_small@})} = \frac{{@num2_val@}}{{@den2_val@}} = {@ta2@}\)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\(\displaystyle \boxed{ \text{Number of sequences} = {@ta2@} }\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
